  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Around Le Lavandou and Bormes-les-Mimosas, dog-friendly options are scarce. Right past the fishermen's huts leading to the Fort de Brégançon, the small pebble beach of Brégançon looks out over Cabasson bay and the Giens peninsula. The Bormes-les-Mimosas tourist office states there that "animals are accepted", and specifies on its beaches page that "our four-legged friends are allowed on the Brégançon and Gouron beaches all year round".</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is on foot only from Cabasson beach, with compulsory paid parking at Parc Capalo, the private car park of the Cabasson and Brégançon beaches (paid from April to October). The tourist office listing (updated on 28 August 2026) specifies that dogs are allowed all year, that they may run freely in the marked area, but that they must be kept on a leash on the access path. The beach is open every day, with toilets, showers, picnic tables and a restaurant nearby.</p>
      <p>Brégançon beach is the small beach to the left of Cabasson beach, right by the Fort. Don't confuse it with <a href="/en/fiche-plage-cabasson-bormes-les-mimosas">Cabasson</a>, 375 metres long and supervised: the tourist office writes on its listing that Cabasson beach is open to dogs from November to March, and that in the summer season they have access to the small Brégançon beach.</p>
      <p>The Fort de Brégançon, summer residence of the Presidents of the Republic, cannot be visited with a dog (tourist office FAQ). Dogs are however admitted on the historic guided tour of the village of Bormes, but not in the town's parks.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: keep your dog on a leash on the access path, as the tourist office asks, and check the coastal path rules before heading further along it.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p><a href="/en/fiche-plage-gouron-bormes-les-mimosas">Gouron beach</a>, where the tourist office says dogs are welcome year-round (the office FAQ specifies: part of the beach), lies at the entrance to the port of Bormes-les-Mimosas, near a picnic area and an outdoor fitness area. For your dog's health care in the commune, the office refers to the Les Mimosas veterinary clinic.</p>
    </div>

